<title>THAILAND: Singer appoints debenture underwriter.</title>
<headline>Singer appoints debenture underwriter.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Singer Thailand Plc on Tuesday appointed Thai Farmers Bank Plc as lead underwriter of 500 million baht ($19.2 million) unsecured debentures, the lead underwriter said.</p>
<p>The debenture will have a coupon rate of 12.35 percent per year and three-year maturity, Thai Farmers said in a statement.</p>
<p>Singer Thailand is majority owned by the Singer Co N.V. and is a major distributor of consumer durable goods in Thailand.</p>
<p>The debenture will be privately issued to a group of investors on May 8, it said.</p>
<p>($1 = 26 baht)</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642</p>
